        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  - CodeBlock (CodeBlock.tsx lines 62-75): wrapper `<div className="w-full my-1 bg-amber-100 border-l-4 border-amber-400 rounded hover:shadow dark:bg-zinc-600 dark:border-zinc-400 relative">`, header row `className="w-full px-2 py-1 flex flex-row justify-between items-center text-amber-500 dark:text-zinc-400"`, then:
    <div className="overflow-auto">
      <pre className={cn("no-wrap overflow-auto", "w-full p-2 bg-amber-50 dark:bg-zinc-700 relative")}>
        <code className={cn(`language-${formatedLanguage}`, "block text-sm leading-5")} dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: highlightedCode }}></code>
      </pre>
    </div>
    Special `__html` language returns `<div className="w-full overflow-auto !my-2" dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: content }} />`; `mermaid` delegates to MermaidBlock.
  - Inline code (Code.tsx):
    <code className="inline break-all px-1 font-mono text-sm rounded opacity-80 bg-gray-100 dark:bg-zinc-700">{content}</code>
  - List (List.tsx): creates `ol`/`ul`/`dl`, class `list-decimal` for ORDERED, `list-disc` for UNORDERED, `list-none` for DESCRIPTION; inline `style={{ paddingLeft: `${indent > 0 ? indent * 10 : 20}px` }}` (task list indent uses `indent * 8`). List items render plain `<li>` (OrderedListItem.tsx / UnorderedListItem.tsx).
  - Blockquote (Blockquote.tsx):
    <blockquote className="p-2 border-s-4 rounded border-gray-300 bg-gray-50 dark:border-gray-500 dark:bg-zinc-700">
  - Link (Link.tsx): MUI Joy `MLink underline="always" target="_blank" href={url} rel="noopener noreferrer">` wrapping `<span onMouseEnter=... onMouseLeave=...>`, with a Joy Tooltip that fetches link metadata on hover. AutoLink also renders Link.
  - Image (Image.tsx): plain `<img src={url} alt={altText} decoding="async" loading="lazy" />`, no class/wrapper.
  - HorizontalRule (HorizontalRule.tsx): MUI Joy `<Divider className="!my-3" />`.
  - Bold/BoldItalic use `<strong>`/`<em>`, Italic uses `<em>`, Strikethrough uses `<del>`, Text uses `<span>`.
- No markdown-specific CSS file exists. Markdown styling is entirely Tailwind utility classes plus browser defaults for `p`, `pre`, `th`, `td`, `li`, `blockquote`, `img`, `table`. `whitespace-pre-wrap` and `word-break` are on the MemoContent content container.

4. Creator/author and created-at/display time on /reader cards.
- Reader.tsx line 16 renders both in one element:
  <p className="reader-meta">{memo.creator} · {memo.displayTime?.toISOString()}</p>
- `memo.creator` is the raw proto string `users/{user}` (Memo.creator field comment in memo_service.ts: "Format: users/{user}"). `displayTime` is `Date|undefined` and is output verbatim as ISO string. Reader does not load the user object/nickname.
- Normal in-app card use `MemoView` with creator nickname and `relative-time`; not used by /reader. Reference classes there: creator link `className="w-full block leading-tight hover:opacity-80 truncate text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400"`, date wrapper `className="w-auto -mt-0.5 text-xs leading-tight text-gray-400 dark:text-gray-500 select-none cursor-pointer"`, and `relative-time datetime={memo.displayTime?.toISOString()} format={relativeTimeFormat}`.

5. Resource/attachment filename display.
- Reader.tsx line 18:
  <div className="reader-attachments">{memo.resources.map(resource => <a key={resource.name} href={resource.externalLink || `/file/${resource.name}/${resource.filename}`}>{resource.filename}</a>)}</div>
- Each attachment is `<a>`, no class, inside `div.reader-attachments`. Href uses `externalLink` if set, else `/file/{resource.name}/{resource.filename}`. Label is `resource.filename`.
- Resource proto fields (resource_service.ts): `name` ("The name of the resource."), `filename`, `externalLink`, `type`, plus more.
- Normal in-app card uses MemoResourceListView (web/src/components/MemoResourceListView.tsx) and MemoResource (web/src/components/MemoResource.tsx). Reference filename element/class in MemoResource.tsx:
  <span className="text-sm max-w-[256px] truncate cursor-pointer" onClick={handlePreviewBtnClick}>
